    choices: [['How does Ms. Hayashi describe the advance?', 'Money paid upfront against future royalties.', 'An extra bonus with no relevant conditions.', 'A'], ['Which royalties are discussed in this condition?', 'Every possible kind of income Kai could ever earn.', 'Additional recording royalties under the proposed terms.', 'B'], ['What is still unspecified?', 'That the advance has conditions.', 'The exact control period and list of costs.', 'B'], ['Which question fits the review?', 'Which expenses are included in recovery?', 'Why should we ignore the clauses?', 'A']],
    mission: { situation: 'You are Kai. Your tutor is Ms. Hayashi. Listen to her new review message. Confirm the difference between the headline payment and its conditions.', task: 'Summarise the recording scope and payment condition, then ask a precise follow-up question.', roles: ['Ms. Hayashi', 'Kai'], title: 'Questions after the first review', text: 'Kai, the attractive payment figure does not tell us everything. In this proposal, the advance is paid against future royalties. Additional recording royalties would follow only after the specified recoupable costs were recovered. Recoupable means recoverable under the agreed terms. We still need to examine the expense details. Also, the control clause concerns the master recordings covered by this agreement. Do not assume it describes every recording you have ever made. Which clause would you like me to explain further?', lines: ['Kai, is the advance simply an extra bonus?', 'What has to happen before additional recording royalties under this proposal?', 'What does recoupable mean in my explanation?', 'Which recordings does the control clause concern?', 'What would you like to clarify about the expense details?'], evidence: 'Private follow-up explains this fictional proposal, not universal law or financial advice. Advance is paid upfront against future royalties; specified recoupable costs precede additional recording royalties under these terms. Do not claim all spending, songwriting royalties, concert income or personal repayment obligations are included. Long control period and cost list have no supplied numbers. Masters covered by proposal are not automatically every existing independent recording.', useful: ['The advance is paid ...', 'Under these terms, ...', 'Additional recording royalties would ...', 'This clause covers ...', 'Could you clarify which ...?'] },
    topics: [['PAYMENT CONDITIONS', ['Why might a headline figure leave questions?', 'How can you check when a later payment begins?', 'What would you ask about an expense list?']], ['CLEAR QUESTIONS', ['How do you ask for a term in simpler English?', 'Why check which items an agreement covers?', 'What can you say if you need more time to understand?']], ['CAREFUL REVIEW', ['What can a specialist help explain?', 'Why keep notes during a review?', 'How can you confirm your understanding afterwards?']]],
